  "question": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{A}, \\mathrm{B}, \\mathrm{C}$ try to hit a target simultaneously but independently. Their respective probabilities of hitting the targets are $\\frac{3}{4}, \\frac{1}{2}, \\frac{5}{8}$. The probability that the target is hit by A or B but not by $\\mathrm{C}$ is :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n$21 / 64$\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$7 / 8$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$7 / 32$\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n$9 / 64$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{A}$ or $\\mathrm{B}$ but not by $\\mathrm{C})=\\mathrm{P}((\\mathrm{A} \\cup \\mathrm{B}) \\cap \\overline{\\mathrm{C}})$\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& =\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{A} \\cup \\mathrm{B}) \\times \\mathrm{P}(\\overline{\\mathrm{C}}) \\\\\n& =[\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{A})+\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{B})-\\mathrm{P}(\\mathrm{A} \\cap \\mathrm{B})] \\times \\mathrm{P}(\\overline{\\mathrm{C}}) \\\\\n& = \\\\\n& {\\left[\\frac{3}{4}+\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{3}{4} \\times \\frac{1}{2}\\right] \\times \\frac{3}{8}=\\left(\\frac{6+4-3}{8}\\right) \\times \\frac{3}{8}=\\frac{21}{64}}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}